<article class="main__article">
    <h2>Our Story</h2>
    <p>It all began on a chilly winter evening in 1990, in the heart of our hometown. Armed with nothing but a tiny stove, an old family recipe, and an unstoppable love for momos, our founder set up a humble roadside stall. Little did he know, these soft, steaming dumplings would soon win the hearts (and tastebuds) of thousands.</p>

    <p>What started as a simple family recipe quickly became a local sensation. People from neighboring towns traveled miles just to grab a plate of our signature momos, hand-folded with love and filled with a secret blend of spices that has been passed down for generations.</p>

    <p>Over the years, our kitchen grew bigger, our menu expanded, but our mission stayed the same — to spread happiness, one momo at a time. From juicy steamed classics to crispy fried delights, every bite at Momo Badshah carries a story, a tradition, and a sprinkle of joy.</p>

    <p>Today, we’re not just a restaurant — we’re a community of momo lovers. Whether you’re here for a quick bite, a family feast, or just to say hello, you’re always part of our momo family.</p>

    <p class="center"><strong>Come join us, and let’s make life a little more delicious!</strong> 🥟✨</p>
